+# Starlab OpenClaw Agent for Windows
+
+This is the Windows desktop target for the Starlab fork of OpenClaw.
+
+It is intentionally placed under `openclaw/apps/windows` so the employee desktop app is built from the OpenClaw source tree, while the central control-plane stays on `https://starlabagent.pp.ua`.
+
+## Flow
+
+1. Николай creates an invite/registration code in the Telegram bot.
+2. The employee launches the Windows app and enters the code.
+3. The app calls `POST /api/v1/device-agents/activate`.
+4. The server returns user, role, device, and device token.
+5. The token is stored through Electron `safeStorage` when available.
+6. The app sends heartbeat every 60 seconds and sends chat messages to `POST /api/v1/local-agent/chat`.
+
+## Build
+
+```powershell
+npm install
+npm run build:win
+```
+
+The artifact is:
+
+```text
+dist/starlab-openclaw-agent-windows.exe
+```
